      "content_markdown": "Example 8. Solve the equations\n$$\\frac{x}{5} + \\frac{3}{y} = 3$$\n$$\\frac{x}{2} - \\frac{6}{y} = 2$$\n\nSolution : The given equations are\n$$\\frac{x}{5} + \\frac{3}{y} = 3.......................... (1)$$\n$$\\frac{x}{2} - \\frac{6}{y} = 2.......................... (2)$$\n\nMultiplying equation (1) by 2 and then adding with equation (2), we get\n$$\\frac{2x}{5} + \\frac{6}{y} = 6.......................... (3)$$\n$$\\frac{x}{2} - \\frac{6}{y} = 2.......................... (4)$$\n\nor, $$\\frac{2x}{5} + \\frac{x}{2} = 8$$\nor, $$\\frac{4x + 5x}{10} = 8$$\nor, $$\\frac{9x}{10} = 8$$\n$$\\therefore x = \\frac{80}{9}$$",
